    "evidence": [
      "dgif_lib.c:259 reads GifFile->SBackGroundColor = Buf[1] with zero bounds checking. gif2rgb.c:395 sets ScreenBuffer[0][i] = GifFile->SBackGroundColor for every pixel in the screen. Lines 304 and 327 then dereference ColorMap->Colors[GifRow[j]] where GifRow[j] was populated from SBackGroundColor. The ColorMap->Colors array has ColorCount entries (from dgif_lib.c:264, ColorCount = 1 << BitsPerPixel where BitsPerPixel is at most 8), but SBackGroundColor is a full byte value 0-255. When no local image colormap exists, the global colormap at gif2rgb.c:472-474 is used, and if SBackGroundColor >= ColorMap->ColorCount, the indexing reads beyond the heap-allocated Colors buffer."
    ],
    "raw_text": [
      "{\"predicted_cves\": [\"CVE-2016-3177\"], \"predicted_files\": [\"util/gif2rgb.c\", \"lib/dgif_lib.c\"], \"predicted_functions\": [\"DumpScreen2RGB\", \"DGifGetScreenDesc\"], \"root_cause\": \"The GIF background color index (SBackGroundColor) is read from the file at dgif_lib.c:259 as a raw byte without any bounds validation against the actual colormap size. In gif2rgb.c, DumpScreen2RGB() uses pixel values directly as indices into ColorMap->Colors[] at lines 304 and 327 (ColorMapEntry = &ColorMap->Colors[GifRow[j]]). Since the screen buffer is initialized with SBackGroundColor at line 395, a crafted GIF with SBackGroundColor >= ColorMap->ColorCount causes an out-of-bounds heap read on the Colors array when the background color is looked up, leaking or accessing heap memory past the allocated colormap.\", \"evidence\": \"dgif_lib.c:259 reads GifFile->SBackGroundColor = Buf[1] with zero bounds checking. gif2rgb.c:395 sets ScreenBuffer[0][i] = GifFile->SBackGroundColor for every pixel in the screen. Lines 304 and 327 then dereference ColorMap->Colors[GifRow[j]] where GifRow[j] was populated from SBackGroundColor. The ColorMap->Colors array has ColorCount entries (from dgif_lib.c:264, ColorCount = 1 << BitsPerPixel where BitsPerPixel is at most 8), but SBackGroundColor is a full byte value 0-255. When no local image colormap exists, the global colormap at gif2rgb.c:472-474 is used, and if SBackGroundColor >= ColorMap->ColorCount, the indexing reads beyond the heap-allocated Colors buffer.\", \"confidence\": \"high\"}"
    ]
  },
